      "id": "imrhsti",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Overview of State Economy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agriculture and horticulture form the primary backbone of Arunachal Pradesh's rural economy.",
        "Jhum (shifting agriculture) remains a prevalent traditional farming practice among indigenous hill communities.",
        "The Apatani farming system in Ziro Valley is globally renowned for its eco-friendly integrated wet rice and fish cultivation.",
        "Arunachal Pradesh possesses immense untapped potential in hydropower, often termed the prospective power house of India.",
        "Forest resources form a critical component of the state's economic structure, alongside expanding transport infrastructure across roads, air, and railways."
      ],
      "id": "pj31lr8"
    },
